cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "stegolab: a research bench for adaptive image steganography and steganalysis"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it."
type: software
# Replace the entity below with your full name and ORCID before publishing.
authors:
  - name: "RE22GDV"
    alias: "RE22GDV"
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-09-02"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/RE22GDV/stegolab"
abstract: >-
  stegolab implements content-adaptive least-significant-bit steganography in
  which the order of embedding positions is derived from an integer complexity
  map of the cover image, so that the receiver reconstructs it without any side
  information. It ships five baseline methods for comparison, an authenticated
  container format, quality and detectability metrics, twelve container attacks,
  classical steganalysis, and a multilingual desktop interface.
keywords:
  - steganography
  - steganalysis
  - adaptive embedding
  - least significant bit
  - reproducible research
